On 18 Jul 2014, Jorgen Grahn wrote:
> How to hide the ghost, though?  Teleporting into a vault and letting
> yourself be killed by a zombie is the option I can think of, but there
> are surely others.

That *is* tricky.  I was imaginging that the victim would be sufficiently
tilted to ragequit before searching the level, so it would suffice to
merely die far from the upstair.  But, many nethackers are made of sterner
stuff as regards what doesn't kill them outright....

The best I can think of is to polymorph to xorn, go to a corner of the
level, unpolymorph and stone yourself.  It's resource intensive, though.

A cheaper idea I had was to dig a pit, read a cursed scroll of earth, and
then self-petrify.  In theory, this should result in your statue being buried
with no trace.  (except potion/spell of detection, of course).  In
(wizard-mode) practice, however, the boulder doesn't fall into the pit --
the devteam didn't think of it.

Another idea that doesn't work is stoning oneself while levitating over the
hole.  In theory your statue should fall out of the level immediately on
load, but in practice the statue just remains on the hole grid square
without falling, as the devteam didn't think of that either.

It does work if you stone yourself while levitating over water.  But water
is rare.  While you can get pools on an ordinary level as a random
fountain effect, that would be proof the level is bones.


Maybe it's best to think out of the box.  You could choose not to hide the
fact that a level is bones, and instead arrange things so that it looks like
you were playing normally and just happened to have bad luck that your
ghost is eager to share.  Such as losing ascension-kit grade armor to an
invisible nymph....

